eta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059545/state.json" "file_sha256" "e2f30200c03ff2c04bc89b5ec3e15ef1342fe19d42294c553761a92bdbd3f00d"} {"question" "q-17113" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ we use the rule\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(\\theta )}{{x}^{′}(\\theta )}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059545/state.json" "file_sha256" "e2f30200c03ff2c04bc89b5ec3e15ef1342fe19d42294c553761a92bdbd3f00d"} {"question" "q-17113" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059545/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ba434e8e5648ca4419bdcce48409f4f84237c3b607c3c3e3061a0e349de04df7"} {"question" "q-17113" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059545/state.json" "file_sha256" "e2f30200c03ff2c04bc89b5ec3e15ef1342fe19d42294c553761a92bdbd3f00d"} {"question" "q-17113" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )"] ["math" "\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }"] ["math" "\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }"] ["math" "\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta "] ["math" "\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta "]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059545/state.json" "file_sha256" "e2f30200c03ff2c04bc89b5ec3e15ef1342fe19d42294c553761a92bdbd3f00d"} {"question" "q-17113" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059545/state.json" "file_sha256" "e2f30200c03ff2c04bc89b5ec3e15ef1342fe19d42294c553761a92bdbd3f00d"} {"question" "q-353226" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059545/assets/064e75694d82bed2177df55e2e66c3343a2c0396cd54f5d4304f952a01abb219.png)\n\nFor the polar curve $r=\\theta $ (shown above) evaluate the derivative $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$   at $\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(\\theta ) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta , \\\\ {x}^{′}(\\theta ) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDo not round the answer.\n\n${\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{\\theta =\\pi /2}=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059545/state.json" "file_sha256" "e2f30200c03ff2c04bc89b5ec3e15ef1342fe19d42294c553761a92bdbd3f00d"} {"question" "q-353226" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use the rule for differentiating parametric equations:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(\\theta )}{{x}^{′}(\\theta )}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the numerator and denominator at $\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =1+\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =0-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{2}} & =\\frac{{y}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{2})}{{x}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{2})} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(-\\frac{\\pi }{2})} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059545/state.json" "file_sha256" "e2f30200c03ff2c04bc89b5ec3e15ef1342fe19d42294c553761a92bdbd3f00d"} {"question" "q-353226" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059545/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ba434e8e5648ca4419bdcce48409f4f84237c3b607c3c3e3061a0e349de04df7"} {"question" "q-353226" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059545/state.json" "file_sha256" "e2f30200c03ff2c04bc89b5ec3e15ef1342fe19d42294c553761a92bdbd3f00d"} {"question" "q-353226" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{2}{\\pi}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059545/state.json" "file_sha256" "e2f30200c03ff2c04bc89b5ec3e15ef1342fe19d42294c553761a92bdbd3f00d"} {"question" "q-353218" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the slope $m$ of the tangent line to the polar curve $r=1+\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\theta )$ at $\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(\\theta ) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\theta )+{sec}^{2}⁡(\\theta ), \\\\ {x}^{′}(\\theta ) & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\theta ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDo not round the answer.\n\n$m=$ \n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059545/state.json" "file_sha256" "e2f30200c03ff2c04bc89b5ec3e15ef1342fe19d42294c553761a92bdbd3f00d"} {"question" "q-353218" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ we use the rule\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(\\theta )}{{x}^{′}(\\theta )}.\n$$\n\nWe have,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{3}) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})+{sec}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}+{2}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}+4 \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{3}) & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nHence, the slope $m$ of the tangent line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m={\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{\\theta =\\pi /3} & =\\frac{{y}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{3})}{{x}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{3})} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{9}{2})}{(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})} \\\\  & =-\\frac{9}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\  & =-3\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059545/state.json" "file_sha256" "e2f30200c03ff2c04bc89b5ec3e15ef1342fe19d42294c553761a92bdbd3f00d"} {"question" "q-353218" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059545/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ba434e8e5648ca4419bdcce48409f4f84237c3b607c3c3e3061a0e349de04df7"} {"question" "q-353218" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059545/state.json" "file_sha256" "e2f30200c03ff2c04bc89b5ec3e15ef1342fe19d42294c553761a92bdbd3f00d"} {"question" "q-353218" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-3\\sqrt{3}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059545/state.json" "file_sha256" "e2f30200c03ff2c04bc89b5ec3e15ef1342fe19d42294c553761a92bdbd3f00d"} {"question" "q-141046" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the slope of the tangent line to the polar curve $r={e}^{2\\theta }$ at $\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ given that\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(\\theta )={e}^{2\\theta }(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ),\\,{x}^{′}(\\theta )={e}^{2\\theta }(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059545/state.json" "file_sha256" "e2f30200c03ff2c04bc89b5ec3e15ef1342fe19d42294c553761a92bdbd3f00d"} {"question" "q-141046" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ we use the rule\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(\\theta )}{{x}^{′}(\\theta )}.\n$$\n\nWe have,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & ={e}^{\\pi /2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{4}+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & ={e}^{\\pi /2}(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}+2\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,{e}^{\\pi /2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & ={e}^{\\pi /2}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{4}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & ={e}^{\\pi /2}(2\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,{e}^{\\pi /2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nHence, the slope of the tangent line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{\\theta =\\pi /4} & =\\frac{{y}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4})}{{x}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4})} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,{e}^{\\pi /2})}{(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,{e}^{\\pi /2})} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059545/state.json" "file_sha256" "e2f30200c03ff2c04bc89b5ec3e15ef1342fe19d42294c553761a92bdbd3f00d"} {"question" "q-141046" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059545/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ba434e8e5648ca4419bdcce48409f4f84237c3b607c3c3e3061a0e349de04df7"} {"question" "q-141046" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059545/state.json" "file_sha256" "e2f30200c03ff2c04bc89b5ec3e15ef1342fe19d42294c553761a92bdbd3f00d"} {"question" "q-141046" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3"] ["math" "3{e}^{\\pi /2}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,{e}^{\\pi /2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059545/state.json" "file_sha256" "e2f30200c03ff2c04bc89b5ec3e15ef1342fe19d42294c553761a92bdbd3f00d"} {"question" "q-141046" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059545/state.json" "file_sha256" "e2f30200c03ff2c04bc89b5ec3e15ef1342fe19d42294c553761a92bdbd3f00d"} {"question" "q-141048" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the polar curve $r=2\\theta $  at $\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ given that\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(\\theta )=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +2\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,{x}^{′}(\\theta )=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -2\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059545/state.json" "file_sha256" "e2f30200c03ff2c04bc89b5ec3e15ef1342fe19d42294c553761a92bdbd3f00d"} {"question" "q-141048" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ we use the rule\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(\\theta )}{{x}^{′}(\\theta )}.\n$$\n\nWe have,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{2}+2(\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{2} \\\\  & =2+0 \\\\  & =2,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{2}-2(\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{2} \\\\  & =0-\\pi  \\\\  & =-\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{\\theta =\\pi /2} & =\\frac{{y}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{2})}{{x}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{2})} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{-\\pi } \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059545/state.json" "file_sha256" "e2f30200c03ff2c04bc89b5ec3e15ef1342fe19d42294c553761a92bdbd3f00d"} {"question" "q-141048" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059545/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ba434e8e5648ca4419bdcce48409f4f84237c3b607c3c3e3061a0e349de04df7"} {"question" "q-141048" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059545/state.json" "file_sha256" "e2f30200c03ff2c04bc89b5ec3e15ef1342fe19d42294c553761a92bdbd3f00d"} {"question" "q-141048" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{2}{\\pi }"] ["math" "-\\pi "] ["math" "2"] ["math" "2\\pi "] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059545/state.json" "file_sha256" "e2f30200c03ff2c04bc89b5ec3e15ef1342fe19d42294c553761a92bdbd3f00d"} {"question" "q-141048" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{2}{\\pi }"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059545/state.json" "file_sha256" "e2f30200c03ff2c04bc89b5ec3e15ef1342fe19d42294c553761a92bdbd3f00d"} {"question" "q-348093" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "For the polar curve $r=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\theta ),$ evaluate the derivative $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at $\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(\\theta ) & =-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\theta )\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\theta )\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta , \\\\ {x}^{′}(\\theta ) & =-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\theta )\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\theta )\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDo not round the answer.\n\n${\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{\\theta \\,=\\,\\pi /4}=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059545/state.json" "file_sha256" "e2f30200c03ff2c04bc89b5ec3e15ef1342fe19d42294c553761a92bdbd3f00d"} {"question" "q-348093" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use the rule for differentiating parametric equations:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(\\theta )}{{x}^{′}(\\theta )}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the numerator and denominator at $\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{4},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =-4\\cdot 0\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})+(-1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}),\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =-4\\cdot 0\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})-(-1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,{|}_{\\theta \\,=\\,\\pi /4} & =\\frac{{y}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4})}{{x}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{4})} \\\\  & =\\frac{-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})} \\\\  & =-\\frac{(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})}{(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})} \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059545/state.json" "file_sha256" "e2f30200c03ff2c04bc89b5ec3e15ef1342fe19d42294c553761a92bdbd3f00d"} {"question" "q-348093" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059545/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ba434e8e5648ca4419bdcce48409f4f84237c3b607c3c3e3061a0e349de04df7"} {"question" "q-348093" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059545/state.json" "file_sha256" "e2f30200c03ff2c04bc89b5ec3e15ef1342fe19d42294c553761a92bdbd3f00d"} {"question" "q-348093" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059545/state.json" "file_sha256" "e2f30200c03ff2c04bc89b5ec3e15ef1342fe19d42294c553761a92bdbd3f00d"} {"question" "q-142369" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059545/assets/40375a9794d9e399327cfcf128e017f05d20319fd86d41a8a9f49e01f58ccae0.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the polar curve $r=4$  (shown above) at $\\theta =\\frac{7\\pi }{4}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059545/state.json" "file_sha256" "e2f30200c03ff2c04bc89b5ec3e15ef1342fe19d42294c553761a92bdbd3f00d"} {"question" "q-142369" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use the formula for differentiating parametric curves:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(\\theta )}{{x}^{′}(\\theta )}\n$$\n\nFirst, we recall that to convert from polar coordinates to Cartesian coordinates, we use\n\n$$\nx=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that $r=4,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculating the necessary derivatives, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(\\theta ) & =-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,{y}^{′}(\\theta )=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta } \\\\ =-\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we arrive at\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{\\theta =7\\pi /4} & =-\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =-(-1) \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059545/state.json" "file_sha256" "e2f30200c03ff2c04bc89b5ec3e15ef1342fe19d42294c553761a92bdbd3f00d"} {"question" "q-142369" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059545/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ba434e8e5648ca4419bdcce48409f4f84237c3b607c3c3e3061a0e349de04df7"} {"question" "q-142369" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059545/state.json" "file_sha256" "e2f30200c03ff2c04bc89b5ec3e15ef1342fe19d42294c553761a92bdbd3f00d"} {"question" "q-142369" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-\\sqrt{3}"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "\\sqrt{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/1